# Process: reaper-sync

USE WHEN you want to execute reaper-sync

## Execution

This process executes a single tool call to synchronize the 00OS contents to the .cursor/rules directory using the PowerShell script. The following flags are supported:

- `--dry-run` or `-DryRun`: Simulate sync, no changes made
- `--detect-orphans` or `-DetectOrphans`: Detect orphaned .mdc files in .cursor/rules
- `--remove-orphans` or `-RemoveOrphans`: Remove orphaned .mdc files in .cursor/rules
- `--verbose` or `-Verbose`: Show detailed sync information

**Tool Call Example:**

```javascript
await tools.call('run_terminal_cmd', {
  command: 'powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File 00reaper/00scripts/Sync-00OS-Complete.ps1 [flags]',
  is_background: false,
  explanation: 'Synchronize 00OS contents to .cursor/rules using PowerShell script with optional flags'
});
```
Replace `[flags]` with any combination of `-DryRun`, `-DetectOrphans`, `-RemoveOrphans`, and `-Verbose` as needed.

## Examples

> reaper-sync
✅ 00OS contents synchronized to .cursor/rules

> reaper-sync --dry-run
✅ Dry run: No changes made, sync actions listed

> reaper-sync --detect-orphans --remove-orphans --verbose
✅ Orphaned rules detected and removed, detailed output shown

> reaper-sync --dry-run --detect-orphans --verbose
✅ Dry run: Orphaned rules detected, detailed output shown, no changes made
